{"step_index":3730,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T10:37:00Z","thinking":"**Investigating JS Errors**\n\nI'm currently focused on that JavaScript error. The code snippet with `gl.getAttribLocation` is the source, it seems. I'm trying to determine why it's failing to retrieve the attribute location. The `gl.vertexAttribPointer` and `gl.vertexAttribDivisor` calls hinge on this, so pinpointing the issue with `io` and `ic` is my priority.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Data Loading Issue**\n\nI've discovered the root cause of the WebGL error. The problem stems from asynchronous data loading.  `draw()` is called before the buffers for `aOffsetScale` and `aColor` are populated via `fetch('ast_nodes.json')`. This results in `gl.drawArraysInstanced` attempting to read from empty buffers, resulting in an \"out of bounds\" error and the render loop's demise. I need to ensure the data is loaded before the initial draw call.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' > /tmp/fix_webgl.py\\nimport re\\n\\npath = '/Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/ops/scripts/fullscreen_ui/sovereign_orbs.html'\\nwith open(path, 'r') as f:\\n    content = f.read()\\n\\n# Make sure buffers are allocated immediately so WebGL doesn't crash on frame 1\\nnew_init = \\\"\\\"\\\"// Load Real Codebase AST Nodes\\nconst INST_COUNT = 100000;\\nlet instData = new Float32Array(INST_COUNT * 4); // x, y, scale, phase\\nlet colorData = new Float32Array(INST_COUNT * 3); // r, g, b\\nconst instBuf = gl.createBuffer();\\nconst colorBuf = gl.createBuffer();\\n\\n// Pre-allocate to prevent WebGL out of bounds error before fetch completes\\ngl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, instBuf);\\ngl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, INST_COUNT * 4 * 4, gl.DYNAMIC_DRAW);\\ngl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, colorBuf);\\ngl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, INST_COUNT * 3 * 4, gl.DYNAMIC_DRAW);\\n\\nlet astLoaded = false;\\nfetch('ast_nodes.json').then(r => r.json()).then(data => {\\n    for(let i=0; i<data.nodes.length; i++) {\\n        let n = data.nodes[i];\\n        instData[i*4+0] = n.x;\\n        instData[i*4+1] = n.y;\\n        instData[i*4+2] = n.scale;\\n        instData[i*4+3] = Math.random() * Math.PI * 2;\\n        colorData[i*3+0] = n.r;\\n        colorData[i*3+1] = n.g;\\n        colorData[i*3+2] = n.b;\\n    }\\n    gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, instBuf);\\n    gl.bufferSubData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, 0, instData);\\n    gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, colorBuf);\\n    gl.bufferSubData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, 0, colorData);\\n    astLoaded = true;\\n});\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\ncontent = re.sub(r\\\"// Load Real Codebase AST Nodes.*?\\\\}\\\\);\\\", new_init, content, flags=re.DOTALL)\\n\\nwith open(path, 'w') as f:\\n    f.write(content)\\nEOF\\npython3 /tmp/fix_webgl.py\"","Cwd":"\"/Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain\"","RequestedTerminalID":"\"\"","RunPersistent":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Fixing WebGL buffer allocation\"","toolSummary":"\"Fix WebGL crash in sovereign_orbs.html\""}}]}
